hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"32","On the opening supplication. Abu Kamil narrated to us that Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to them; Imran ibn Muslim Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he rose at night intending to pray tahajjud, would say before the takbir: There is no god but Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, Most Great. I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his poetry, and his pride. He said: Then he would say: Allah is Greatest; and Imran raised his hands, demonstrating."
"33","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, al-Haytham narrated to us, from Thawr, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Tawus, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his right hand over his left hand, then press them both upon his chest while in prayer."
